==Merged second translation== {{otheruses||{{ill|Dir En Grey|ja|DIR EN GREY|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Dir En Grey|qq=}}'s {{ill|Music Video|ja|ミュージック・ビデオ|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Music Video|qq=}}|鬼門 (映像作品)}} '''Kimon''' (鬼門) refers to the northeastern direction ({{ill|Ushitora|ja|艮|1=Gen (Bagua)|2=ja|3=艮|lt=Gen (艮)|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ushitora|qq=}}, "Ox and Tiger": between the {{ill|Ox|ja|丑|1=Ox (Zodiac)|lt=Ox (丑)|2=ja|3=丑|1=Ox (zodiac)|lt=Ox (丑)|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ox|13=User:Immanuelle/Ox (zodiac)|qq=}} and {{ill|Tiger|ja|寅|1=Tiger (Zodiac)|lt=Tiger (寅)|2=ja|3=寅|1=Tiger (zodiac)|lt=Tiger (寅)|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Tiger|13=User:Immanuelle/Tiger (zodiac)|qq=}} on the Chinese zodiac). In Japan, this direction has traditionally been considered ominous and is associated with the entrance and exit of demons.
== Overview ==
The direction opposite to Kimon, the southwest ({{ill|Kon|ja|坤|1=Kun (Bagua)|2=ja|3=坤|lt=Kun (坤)|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kon|qq=}}, {{ill|Hinoeuma|ja|未申|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hinoeuma|qq=}}), is called '''Urakimon''' (裏鬼門) and is similarly regarded as inauspicious. Kimon (northeast) is associated with "demon gate," while the southwest (Urakimon) is referred to as "people gate" or "illness gate," the southeast ({{ill|Sun|ja|巽|1=Xun (Bagua)|2=ja|3=巽|lt=Xun (巽)|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Sun|qq=}}) as "wind gate," and the northwest as "heaven gate" according to {{ill|Onmyōdō|ja|陰陽道|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Onmyōdō|qq=}}.<ref>{{Cite book|title=日本人なら知っておきたい正しい家相の本|author=小池康寿|publisher=プレジデント社|year=2015|page=37}}</ref> In the {{ill|Konjaku Monogatari|ja|今昔物語集|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Konjaku Monogatari|qq=}}, an {{ill|Onmyōji|ja|陰陽師|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Onmyōji|qq=}} named {{ill|Yuge no Koreo|ja|弓削是雄|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Yuge no Koreo|qq=}} predicts an assassin's presence in the northeast direction of {{ill|Tomonokimi Yotsugi|ja|伴宿禰世継|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Tomonokimi Yotsugi|qq=}}’s residence, illustrating a perception of艮as an unlucky direction.<ref>{{Cite book|author=村山修一|title=日本陰陽道史話|publisher=平凡社|year=1988|page=101|ISBN=4-582-76406-1}}</ref> In {{ill|Taiwan|ja|台湾|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Taiwan|qq=}}, Kimon is considered the "gateway between this world and the next," opening during the {{ill|Ghost Month|ja|鬼月|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ghost Month|qq=}} in the seventh lunar month.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://jp.taiwantoday.tw/news.php?unit=190&post=103467|title=「鬼月」と呼ばれるLunisolar Julyの意味|work=TAIWAN TODAY|date=2016-08-12}}</ref>
== Reasons for Fearing Kimon ==
The term "Kimon" appears in the Eastern Han period's {{ill|Wang Chong|ja|王充|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Wang Chong|qq=}}’s ''{{ill|Lunheng|ja|論衡|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Lunheng|qq=}}'', in the ''Correcting Ghosts'' chapter, citing the ''{{ill|Classic of Mountains and Seas|ja|山海経|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Classic of Mountains and Seas|qq=}}''.<ref>{{Cite book|author=水野杏紀|title=易、風水、暦、養生、処世 東アジアの宇宙観|publisher=講談社選書メチエ|year=2016|pages=28-29}}</ref>
